  "goodToKnow": "Die Chemotherapie (colloquially die Chemo) is chemotherapy, treatment of cancer with drugs that kill fast-growing cells. Paul Ehrlich, a German Nobel laureate, coined the term Chemotherapie around 1906 and developed Salvarsan, an early targeted drug. Die Strahlentherapie is radiotherapy, and die Onkologie oncology. Plural: die Chemotherapien."
